From 161b0e7205b0fc26e0d081eb94d41955e5d1e6d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:24:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Playwright browser tests for the web front end

tests/browser drives the real web/index.html and web/app.js in headless
Chromium. The server is not started: tests/browser/fake_api.py answers /query,
/reset, /sectors and /documents with canned replies (including a held /query
for the busy state), records what the page sent, and blocks every other
request. No API key, Qdrant or models are needed.

27 tests plus one strict xfail cover: streamed progress and answer, markdown,
the request body (prompt, session id, ticked sectors), citation links (https
only, target and rel), tidied titles, error / empty / failed replies, the busy
state and double-send guard, Reset, the citations toggle, remembered sectors,
text-not-markup for questions and citation fields, and phone-width overflow.
Each test was checked by breaking app.js on purpose and confirming it fails.

test_html_in_an_answer_does_not_run is xfail(strict=True): app.js sets
innerHTML from marked.parse(answer) without sanitising it, so HTML in an
answer runs. The marker comes off when that is fixed.

Supporting changes:
- app.js sets data-testid on user turn, assistant turn, citation card,
  progress box and error block (index.html cache-buster bumped to v=13)
- tests/browser/vendor holds marked 18.1.3 (MIT) so tests do not depend on
  the CDN the page loads it from
- pytest-playwright added to the dev group (uv.lock updated, nothing else
  bumped); new `browser` marker, excluded from the default run
- ci.yml gets a second job: install Chromium, run -m browser, keep
  screenshots and traces of failures as an artifact
- docs/testing_and_ci.md covers running them and the known gap

